# L §2.3 parse rule 4 (round 8): after `value(...) in CUR by p`, "keys or fields after its by p belong to p". eurkonto
# holds 100.00 EUR on 2026-06-30 (bought 2026-03-02); quote[2026-06] = (close: 4.5, open: 4.1 PLN/EUR). f1: by the
# field close of the keyed read, 100 x 4.5 = 450 PLN (L §5.10 Value: value multiplies exactly). f2: the field open
# belongs to p and the comparison to the whole value: 100 x 4.1 = 410 PLN > lim (400 PLN), true.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

kind fx_buys: event certain
  leg eur: EUR
  leg cash: PLN

input eur_px[m in months]: num PLN/EUR
input base_px: num PLN/EUR
input lim: num PLN
input quote[m in months]: (close num PLN/EUR, open num PLN/EUR)
input buy_day: date
input eur_amt: money EUR
input pln_amt: money PLN

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place eurkonto: accounts EUR lives 2026-01-01..
place market: outside lives 1900-01-01..

def worth[d in days]: num PLN = value(eurkonto, d) in PLN by eur_px[month_of(d)] at d
def px_def[u in currencies]: num PLN/u = base_px

move buy: fx_buys
  on buy_day
  leg eur from market to eurkonto amount eur_amt
  leg cash from konto to market amount pln_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  base_px = 4 PLN/EUR
  lim = 400 PLN
  buy_day = 2026-03-02
  eur_amt = 100.00 EUR
  pln_amt = 425.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  opening[eurkonto] = 0 EUR at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version px
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  eur_px[2026-06] = 4.25 PLN/EUR
  quote[2026-06] = (close: 4.5 PLN/EUR, open: 4.1 PLN/EUR)

ask f1: value(eurkonto, 2026-06-30) in PLN by quote[2026-06].close
ask f2: value(eurkonto, 2026-06-30) in PLN by quote[2026-06].open > lim
=== expect
f1: 450 PLN
...
f2: true
...
